  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "1v1: steer them to the corner",
  "description": "Two groups, each with a cone a little outside the penalty area: X (defenders) on the left with the balls, A (attackers) on the right. A goalkeeper is in goal.\n\nX passes to A, who skates towards the ball. A receives, rounds their cone and attacks the goal. At the same time X rounds their cone and meets them. The attacker tries to get past and finish; the defender skates with them in an arc and steers them out towards the corner flag, away from the goal. Rotation: X goes to A and A to X.\n\nCompetition: a point to the defender if the attacker is forced into the corner without getting a shot off. Switch sides after a while. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The defender takes the inside line, between the attacker and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Never let the attacker get behind you – better a little too far out than beaten on the inside."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Skate with them in an arc and steer – do not charge straight at the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The attacker uses speed and a dummy to get in towards the middle."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
